    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0104" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d14-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-28">28 June 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Former Naval Person to President.
                    Personal and secret. No. 334.</p>
                <p>I send you first of all the very unpleasant reply I have received from U. J. and my rejoinder.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d14-f2"
                    /> This certainly has its bearing on your proposal to meet him alone and I shall
                    not seek to deter you if you can get him to come.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d14-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d14-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission not indicated.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d14-f2" n="2" xml:id="d14-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed herein. The exchange concerned the second front.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
